---
const stack = [
  { label: 'AI', items: ['Groq', 'Llama 3.3 70B', 'Tool-calling', 'Schema-constrained extraction'] },
  { label: 'Backend', items: ['Python', 'FastAPI', 'Pydantic', 'Docker'] },
  { label: 'Frontend', items: ['Next.js', 'TypeScript', 'Recharts', 'Motion'] },
  { label: 'Data', items: ['EU CBAM Regulation 2023/956', 'Reg (EU) 2025/2621', 'Dir (EU) 2023/959', 'DG TAXUD'] },
];
---

<section class="about section" id="about">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="marker">
      <span class="num">04</span>
      <span class="marker-dot"></span>
      <span>About</span>
    </div>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-left">
        <h2 class="display about-heading">
          EU importers pay carbon tax from <em>2026</em>. Their suppliers send <em>messy evidence</em>. CarbonLenz turns that mess into money.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about-right">
        <p class="about-body">
          The EU Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM) starts its definitive phase in 2026. Importers of iron &amp; steel, cement, aluminium, fertilisers, hydrogen, and electricity must declare embedded emissions and surrender CBAM certificates. If the supplier's evidence is incomplete or unverified, the importer falls onto punitive EU default values — and pays more.
        </p>
        <p class="about-body">
          CarbonLenz uses AI to read supplier evidence, extract the CBAM fields, check what's missing, and calculate the financial gap between the forced default and the achievable-if-verified cost — across the full 2026–2034 phase-in ramp. All calculations use official EU data with source citations.
        </p>

        <div class="stack">
          {stack.map((row) => (
            <div class="stack-row">
              <span class="stack-label micro">{row.label}</span>
              <div class="stack-items">
                {row.items.map((item) => (
                  <span class="pill">{item}</span>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 80px);
  }

  .about-heading {
    font-size: clamp(44px, 5.5vw, 80px);
    line-height: 1.0;
  }

  .about-body {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .stack {
    margin-top: 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .stack-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .stack-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .stack-label {
    padding-top: 1px;
  }

  .stack-items {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .stack-row {
      grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>